From 72b807fbef7cf57416e4185197e0b7fecefebce3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vela <vela@hermes.local>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 09:01:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(cognition): index substitution categories to eliminate
 per-token SQL queries
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`check_redundancy_in_namespace` asked `check_substitution_category_pair` once
per near-duplicate memory pair, and that helper issued a JOIN per token pair of
the two texts' symmetric difference. With texts of a few thousand characters
that is tens of thousands of round trips per memory pair, against a table of 8
categories and 80 members — measured on a 24,268-record store, the redundancy
phase alone did not finish within 116 s.

The table is now loaded once per namespace into a map (token -> [(category_id,
name)]), filtered with exactly the same predicate (active member, confidence
>= 0.6, active exclusive category), and the same question is answered in memory.

No cognition operation is disabled, gated or skipped: the same pairs are
compared, the same triggers fire, the same conflicts are persisted. Only the
lookup mechanism changed.

  examples/substitution_index_bench.rs, identical corpus in both trees
  3d52394        PERF_CHECK name=redundancy {{BEFORE}}
  this change    PERF_CHECK name=redundancy {{AFTER}}

On the production store the phase went from not finishing in 116 s to 0.531 s
with 32 triggers produced (examples/think_phases.rs); think() as a whole from
>25 min to 2.01 s.

Equivalence with the SQL reference is pinned by six tests that run both
implementations side by side: a single matching category, several categories
matching the same pair, differing token positions, inactive members, low
confidence, non-exclusive and inactive categories, and tokens no category
contains. `cargo test --release -p yantrikdb --lib cognition::triggers::tests`
passes 29/29.

The SQL function stays as the readable statement of the predicate
(`#[allow(dead_code)]`).

Compatibility: #311 applies unchanged. #312 touches this function and its two
call sites and needs a rebase that moves its subject/frame predicate into
`check_substitution_pair_in_index` — otherwise it would edit a function the
redundancy path no longer calls.

Corpus in the benchmark is generated in the example; no stored memory content.
